','Runtime Error','Compile Error','No abnormally found','D',5),(3329,'What is the primary purpose of Data Abstraction?','choose','To allow developers to know all internal implementation details.','To prevent the use of Abstract Data Types (ADTs).','To separate the implementation details of a data type from its interface.','To keep the code in a procedural format.','C',10),(3330,'What is an Abstract Data Type (ADT) defined by?','choose','Its specific implementation details.','The operations it supports.','The number of memory addresses it uses.','Its compilation time.','B',10),(3331,'What is the best definition for a Data Structure?','choose','A method for static memory allocation only.','A way of organizing and storing data in a computer so that it can be accessed and modified efficiently.','A synonym for Object-Oriented Programming.','An algorithm used to compute a Hash function.','B',9),(3332,'Which of the following is NOT a common Data Structure listed in the definition?','choose','Arrays.','Linked Lists.','Queues.','Hyperparameters.','D',9),(3333,'What is the main condition for a Binary Search Tree (BST) structure?','choose','Every node must have exactly three children.','All nodes appear in the order of insertion.','All nodes in the left subtree are less than the node, and those in the right subtree are greater.','The tree only allows slow insertion and deletion.','C',9),(3334,'What is the primary benefit of the BST structure?','choose','It minimizes memory usage.','It allows for fast searching, insertion, and deletion of elements.','It guarantees O(1) time complexity for all operations.','It is the simplest tree structure.','B',9),(3335,'What is the characteristic of Dynamic Data Structures?','choose','Their size is fixed and determined at compilation time.','They do not require the use of pointers.','They can change in size during the execution of a program.','Their performance is always slower than static data structures.','C',9),(3336,'How are Dynamic Data 