es the Control Plane from the Data Plane and allows programmatic control of the network.','It is limited to use only in LANs.','It requires the use of Virtual Reality.','B',13),(3465,'What are Virtual Network Functions (VNFs)?','choose','Hardware-based network functions only.','Software-based network functions running on virtualized infrastructure.','Functions that require the use of Data Level Parallelism.','Functions limited to use only in WAN.','B',13),(3466,'What is the purpose of IP Addressing?','choose','To provide addresses to processors in the CPU.','To uniquely identify devices on a computer network.','To perform asymmetric encryption.','To manage virtual memory.','B',13),(3467,'What is the purpose of IP Subnetting?','choose','To increase network load.','To divide a larger IP network into smaller subnets for more efficient use of IP addresses and network management.','To prevent the use of IPv6.','To eliminate the need for routers.','B',13),(3468,'What is Network Routing?','choose','The process of transmitting data packets only through switches.','The process of selecting the optimal path for data packets from source to destination on a network.','A method for file management.','A method for organizing data structures.','B',13),(3469,'What is the worst-case time complexity of Merge Sort?','choose','O(n)','O(n log n)','O(n^2)','O(log n)','B',8),(3470,'Which algorithm is used to find the shortest path in a graph with positive edge weights?','choose','Depth First Search (DFS)','Prim\'s Algorithm','Dijkstra\'s Algorithm','Bellman-Ford Algorithm','C',8),(3471,'What data structure does Breadth First Search (BFS) use efficiently?','choose','Stack','Queue','Heap','Tree','B',8),(3472,'What is the best-case time complexity of Bubble Sort (when the array is already sorted)?','choose','O(n)','O(n^2)','O(log n)','O(1)','A',8),(3473,'Which of the following is a Divide and Conquer algorithm?','choose','Bubble Sort','Selection Sort','Merge Sort','Insertion Sort','C',8),(3474,'In Binary Search, what is the requirement for the input array?','choose','It must be sorted.','It must contain integers only.','It must be unsorted.','It must have an odd number of elements.','A',8),(3475,'What is the time complexity of accessing an element in an array by index?','choose','O(n)','O(log n)','O(1)','O(n log n)','C',8),(3476,'Which sorting algorithm is known for being efficient on small datasets but inefficient on large ones?','choose','Merge Sort','Quick Sort','Insertion Sort','Heap Sort','C',8),(3477,'What is the main difference between Prim\'s and Kruskal\'s algorithms?','choose','Prim\'s builds a tree, Kruskal\'s builds a forest.','Prim\'s is for sorting, Kruskal\'s is for searching.','Kruskal\'s uses a Stack, Prim\'s uses a Queue.','Prim\'s works on directed graphs only.','A',8),(3478,'What is the space complexity of Merge Sort?','choose','O(1)','O(n)','O(log n)','O(n^2)','B',8),(3479,'Which algorithm is commonly used for cycle detection in a graph?','choose','Binary Search','Floyd\'s Cycle-Finding Algorithm','Dijkstra\'s Algorithm','KMP Algorithm','B',8),(3480,'What is the primary characteristic of a Greedy Algorithm?','choose','It looks at all possible solutions.','It makes the locally optimal choice at each step.','It divides the problem into overlapping subproblems.','It uses recursion extensively.','B',8),(3481,'What problem does the Bellman-Ford algorithm solve that Dijkstra cannot?','choose','Shortest path in unweighted graphs.','Graphs with negative edge weights.','Finding the Maximum Spanning Tree.','Sorting graph nodes.','B',8),(3482,'Which data structure is primarily used to implement Recursion?','choose','Queue','Stack','Linked List','Hash Table','B',8),(3483,'What is the time complexity of inserting an element into a Binary Heap?','choose','O(1)','O(n)','O(log n)','O(n log n)','C',8),(3484,'Which searching algorithm is best suited for an unsorted list?','choose','Binary Search','Linear Search','Interpolation Search','Exponential Search','B',8),(3485,'What is the Knapsack Problem an example of?','choose','Greedy Algorithm','Dynamic Programming','Divide and Conquer','Backtracking','B',8),(3486,'In Big O notation, which represents the slowest growth rate?','choose','O(1)','O(n)','O(n^2)','O(log n)','A',8),(3487,'What is the pivot element in Quick Sort used for?','choose','To divide the array into two sub-arrays.','To store the sorted result.','To count the number of elements.','To find the maximum value.','A',8),(3488,'Which graph traversal algorithm uses a Stack?','choose','BFS','DFS','Dijkstra','Prim','B',8),(3489,'What is a Hash Table primarily used for?','choose','Sorting elements.','Fast data retrieval based on keys.','Storing data hierarchically.','Managing CPU processes.','B',9),(3490,'What is a collision in a Hash Table?','choose','When the table is full.','When two different keys hash to the same index.','When a key cannot be found.','When the hash function returns null.','B',9),(3491,'Which data structure allows insertion and deletion from both ends?','choose','Stack','Queue','Deque','Priority Queue','C',9),(3492,'What is the main advantage of a Linked List over an Array?','choose','Random access is faster.','Dynamic size.','Less memory usage.','Better cache locality.','B',9),(3493,'What is a Full Binary Tree?','choose','A tree where every node has 0 or 2 children.','A tree where all leaves are at the same level.','A tree where every node has exactly 1 child.','A tree that is perfectly balanced.','A',9),(3494,'What is an AVL Tree?','choose','A self-balancing Binary Search Tree.','A tree with n nodes and n-1 edges.','A type of Heap.','A tree used for data compression.','A',9),(3495,'What is the worst-case height of a Binary Search Tree with n nodes?','choose','O(log n)','O(n)','O(1)','O(n log n)','B',9),(3496,'Which data structure is best for implementing Undo/Redo functionality?','choose','Queue','Stack','Tree','Graph','B',9),(3497,'What is a Trie data structure used for?','choose','S