etwork protocol.','A',12),(3520,'What is an Orphan Process?','choose','A process whose parent has terminated.','A process without a name.','A process that cannot be killed.','A process created by the kernel.','A',12),(3521,'What is RAID used for?','choose','Boosting CPU speed.','Data redundancy and performance improvement in storage.','Managing RAM.','Encrypting network traffic.','B',12),(3522,'What does \'Preemptive Multitasking\' mean?','choose','The OS allocates time slices to processes and can interrupt them.','Processes decide when to yield the CPU.','Only one process runs at a time.','The CPU never interrupts a running process.','A',12),(3523,'What is a Page Fault?','choose','An error in a web page.','When a program accesses a page not currently in main memory.','A hardware failure in RAM.','A printer error.','B',12),(3524,'What is the Banker\'s Algorithm used for?','choose','Sorting bank accounts.','Deadlock avoidance.','Calculating interest.','Process scheduling.','B',12),(3525,'What is Encapsulation?','choose','Hiding the internal state and requiring all interaction to be performed through an object\'s methods.','Inheriting from multiple classes.','Using global variables.','Writing code in C++.','A',10),(3526,'What keyword is used to inherit a class in Java?','choose','implements','inherits','extends','using','C',10),(3527,'What is Method Overloading?','choose','Defining multiple methods with the same name but different parameters.','Redefining a method in a subclass.','Calling a method recursively.','Deleting a method.','A',10),(3528,'What is Method Overriding?','choose','Defining a method with the same name and signature in a subclass as in the superclass.','Creating a new method in a subclass.','Changing the return type of a method.','Overloading a method.','A',10),(3529,'What is an Interface?','choose','A class with implemented methods.','A reference type that can contain only constants, method signatures, default methods, and static methods.','A graphi