at is the main advantage of an Adjacency List over an Adjacency Matrix?','choose','Faster access to specific edges.','Uses less memory for sparse graphs.','Easier to implement.','Better for dense graphs.','B',9),(3566,'What is \'Chaining\' in Hash Tables?','choose','A method to link multiple tables.','A collision resolution technique using linked lists.','Connecting to a server.','Encrypting the keys.','B',9),(3567,'What is a Complete Binary Tree?','choose','A tree where every level is fully filled, except possibly the last which is filled from left to right.','A tree with no missing nodes.','A tree where every node has 2 children.','A tree that is red and black.','A',9),(3568,'What does \'LIFO\' stand for?','choose','Last-In, First-Out.','Left-In, First-Out.','Last-In, Fast-Out.','Low-Input, Full-Output.','A',9),(3569,'What is the difference between an Array and an ArrayList (in Java)?','choose','Arrays have fixed size, ArrayLists are dynamic.','Arrays store objects, ArrayLists store primitives.','ArrayLists are faster.','There is no difference.','A',9),(3570,'What is the degree of a node in a tree?','choose','The number of children it has.','Its height.','Its depth.','The value it stores.','A',9),(3571,'Which data structure is used in Breadth-First Search?','choose','Stack','Queue','Heap','Array','B',9),(3572,'What is the time complexity of deleting a node from a Doubly Linked List if the node is given?','choose','O(n)','O(log n)','O(1)','O(n^2)','C',9),(3573,'What is a Priority Queue?','choose','A queue where elements are removed based on priority, not insertion order.','A queue that is faster.','A queue for VIP users.','A stack with priority.','A',9),(3574,'What is Open Addressing in Hash Tables?','choose','A collision resolution strategy where alternative cells are probed.','Allowing anyone to access the table.','Using a linked list for collisions.','Deleting the table.','A',9),(3575,'What is a Leaf node?','choose','The root node.','A node with no children.','A