,'Trees cannot store data.','B',9),(3651,'What is an Adjacency Matrix?','choose','A 2D array used to represent a graph.','A list of neighbors.','A matrix for solving linear equations.','A database table.','A',9),(3652,'For a dense graph, which representation is usually preferred?','choose','Adjacency List','Adjacency Matrix','Edge List','Hash Map','B',9),(3653,'What is a Bloom Filter?','choose','A probabilistic data structure to test whether an element is a member of a set.','A filter for images.','A sorting algorithm.','A type of tree.','A',9),(3654,'Does a Bloom Filter have false negatives?','choose','Yes, always.','No, never.','Sometimes.','Only if empty.','B',9),(3655,'Does a Bloom Filter have false positives?','choose','Yes, possibly.','No, never.','Only for integers.','Only for strings.','A',9),(3656,'What is a Deque?','choose','A double-ended queue.','A decoding algorithm.','A type of SQL query.','A broken queue.','A',9),(3657,'What is a Skip List?','choose','A probabilistic data structure that allows fast search within an ordered sequence of elements.','A list that skips every second element.','A type of array.','A slow linked list.','A',9),(3658,'What is the primary use of a B+ Tree?','choose','Database indexing.','Storing binary files.','Sorting integers.','Graph traversal.','A',9),(3659,'In a Max-Heap, the value of each node is:','choose','Greater than or equal to the values of its children.','Less than its children.','Equal to its parent.','Random.','A',9),(3660,'What is the time complexity to get the minimum element from a Min-Heap?','choose','O(1)','O(log n)','O(n)','O(n log n)','A',9),(3661,'Which data structure is best for implementing a LRU Cache?','choose','Queue','Stack','HashMap + Doubly Linked List','Array','C',9),(3662,'What is the diameter of a tree?','choose','The number of nodes.','The longest path between any two nodes in the tree.','The width of the root.','The number of leaves.','B',9),(3663,'What is \'Starvation\' in process scheduling?','choose','When a process runs out of memory.','When a low-priority process never gets CPU time because of high-priority processes.','When the CPU is idle.','When a process terminates.','B',12),(3664,'What is \'Aging\' in scheduling?','choose','A technique to gradually increase the priority of waiting processes to prevent starvation.','Process termination due to timeout.','Deleting old files.','Updating the OS version.','A',12),(3665,'What is a Monolithic Kernel?','choose','A kernel where all services run in kernel space.','A kernel where services run in user space.','A small kernel.','A kernel for mobile phones.','A',12),(3666,'What is a Microkernel?','choose','A kernel where most services run in user space to increase stability.','A huge kernel.','A kernel for mainframes.','A single file kernel.','A',12),(3667,'What is \'Throughput\' in an OS?','choose','The number of processes completed per unit time.','The speed of the internet.','The size of RAM.','The boot time.','A',12),(3668,'What is \'Turnaround Time\'?','choose','The time taken to boot.','The total time taken from submission of a process to its completion.','The time the CPU is idle.','The time a process waits in the queue.','B',12),(3669,'What is a \'Spinlock\'?','choose','A lock where the thread simply waits in a loop (\'spins\') repeatedly checking until the lock becomes available.','A hard disk spinning.','A secure password.','A type of deadlock.','A',12),(3670,'What is \'Convoy Effect\'?','choose','When a long process holds the CPU, blocking many short processes.','When processes run in parallel.','When network packets are lost.','When the disk is full.','A',12),(3671,'Which scheduling algorithm minimizes average waiting time?','choose','FCFS','Round Robin','Shortest Job First (SJF)','Priority','C',12),(3672,'What is \'Hard Real-Time\' system?','choose','A system where missing a deadline is a total system failure.','A system that is hard to use.','A system with hard drives.','A slow system.','A',12),(