d protected file.','A system file.','A',12),(3683,'What is the Strategy Pattern?','choose','A pattern that defines a family of algorithms and makes them interchangeable.','A strategy for winning games.','A way to organize classes.','A database strategy.','A',10),(3684,'What is the Decorator Pattern?','choose','A pattern used to add new functionality to an object dynamically without altering its structure.','A pattern for UI design.','A pattern to decorate code.','A pattern to remove methods.','A',10),(3685,'What is the Adapter Pattern?','choose','A pattern that allows incompatible interfaces to work together.','A power adapter.','A pattern to adapt screen size.','A pattern to connect to a database.','A',10),(3686,'What is the \'L\' in SOLID principles?','choose','Liskov Substitution Principle.','Loop Principle.','Logic Principle.','Least Privilege.','A',10),(3687,'What does the Liskov Substitution Principle state?','choose','Objects of a superclass should be replaceable with objects of its subclasses without breaking the application.','Code should be readable.','Loops should be short.','Classes should be large.','A',10),(3688,'What is Dependency Injection?','choose','A technique where an object receives other objects that it depends on.','Injecting code into a running process.','A virus injection.','Depending on external libraries.','A',10),(3689,'What is an \'Inner Class\'?','choose','A class defined within another class.','A class that is private.','A class inside a jar file.','A system class.','A',10),(3690,'What is a \'Lambda Expression\' (in Java/C++)?','choose','A short block of code which takes in parameters and returns a value (anonymous function).','A math formula.','A Greek letter.','A variable type.','A',10),(3691,'What is \'Reflection\' in Java?','choose','An API to examine or modify the behavior of methods, classes, and interfaces at runtime.','Seeing yourself in the screen.','Backing up data.','Repeating code.','A',10),(3692,'What is \'Serialization\'?