nd a Queue?','choose','Stack is FIFO, Queue is LIFO.','Stack is LIFO, Queue is FIFO.','Both are FIFO.','Both are LIFO.','B',9),(3755,'What is an \'Associative Array\'?','choose','An array indexed by integers only.','A data structure that maps keys to values (like a Map or Dictionary).','A sorted array.','A 2D array.','B',9),(3756,'What is \'RAID 0\' known for?','choose','Disk Mirroring.','Disk Striping (performance).','Parity.','Fault tolerance.','B',12),(3757,'What is \'RAID 1\' known for?','choose','Disk Mirroring (redundancy).','Disk Striping.','Parity.','High speed only.','A',12),(3758,'What is a \'Context Switch\'?','choose','Switching the monitor on/off.','Saving the state of a running process and loading another.','Changing the user password.','Rebooting the system.','B',12),(3759,'Which scheduler is responsible for selecting a process from disk and loading it into memory?','choose','Short-term scheduler.','Long-term scheduler.','Medium-term scheduler.','I/O scheduler.','B',12),(3760,'Which scheduler selects a process from the ready queue to execute on the CPU?','choose','Short-term scheduler (CPU scheduler).','Long-term scheduler.','Medium-term scheduler.','Disk scheduler.','A',12),(3761,'What is \'Busy Waiting\'?','choose','When a process sleeps while waiting.','When a process repeatedly checks a condition in a loop, consuming CPU.','When the CPU is idle.','When a process is terminated.','B',12),(3762,'What is the \'Banker\'s Algorithm\' used for?','choose','Deadlock Avoidance.','Deadlock Detection.','Memory Allocation.','CPU Scheduling.','A',12),(3763,'What is a \'Page Fault\'?','choose','An error on a webpage.','When a program attempts to access a page not currently in RAM.','A hardware crash.','A printer error.','B',12),(3764,'What is \'Thrashing\'?','choose','High CPU utilization.','Excessive swapping of pages between memory and disk, reducing performance.','Fast execution of code.','A type of virus.','B',12),(3765,'What is \'Virtual Memory\'?','choose','Memory on the GPU.','An abstraction that gives the illusion of a large main memory using disk space.','A small fast memory.','Memory in the cloud.','B',12),(3766,'What is a \'Semaphore\'?','choose','A signaling mechanism for synchronization between processes.','A type of file.','A CPU register.','A network protocol.','A',12),(3767,'What is \'Mutex\' (Mutual Exclusion Object)?','choose','A key that allows only one thread to access a resource at a time.','A shared variable.','A type of deadlock.','A scheduler.','A',12),(3768,'What is \'Starvation\'?','choose','When a process never gets to execute because lower priority processes keep running.','When a process never gets to execute because higher priority processes keep running.','When memory is full.','When the disk is empty.','B',12),(3769,'What is the \'Critical Section\' problem?','choose','Ensuring that only one process executes in its critical section at a time.','Allocating critical memory.','Handling critical errors.','Booting the kernel.','A',12),(3770,'What is \'Aging\' in the context of scheduling?','choose','Replacing old hardware.','Gradually increasing the priority of a waiting process to prevent starvation.','Deleting old files.','Updating the kernel.','B',12),(3771,'What is the \'Interface Segregation Principle\' (ISP)?','choose','Interfaces should be large and comprehensive.','Clients should not be forced to depend on interfaces they do not use.','Classes should inherit from multiple sources.','Code should be segregated into folders.','B',10),(3772,'What is the \'Dependency Inversion Principle\' (DIP)?','choose','High-level modules should not depend on low-level modules; both should depend on abstractions.','Low-level modules should depend on high-level modules.','Dependencies should be hard-coded.','Avoid using interfaces.','A',10),(3773,'What is the \'Singleton\' pattern?','choose','A pattern ensuring a class has only one instance and provides a global point of access to it.','A class with a single method.','A pattern for single-threaded apps.','A pattern for database tables.','A',10),(3774,'What is the \'Observer\' pattern?','choose','A one-to-many dependency where one object notifies others of state changes.','A pattern for watching videos.','A security pattern.','A database pattern.','A',10),(3775,'What is the \'Factory Method\' pattern?','choose','A pattern that defines an interface for creating an object, but lets subclasses alter the type of objects that will be created.','A factory for building hardware.','A method that returns void.','A pattern for deleting objects.','A',10),(3776,'What is \'Encapsulation\'?','choose','Bundling data and methods that operate on that data within a single unit (class) and restricting access.','Exposing all data to the public.','Inheriting from other classes.','Using multiple files.','A',10),(3777,'What is \'Abstraction\'?','choose','Showing only essential features of an object and hiding complexity.','Making code abstract art.','Using complex variable names.','Writing comments.','A',10),(3778,'What is \'Polymorphism\'?','choose','The ability of different classes to be treated as instances of the same general class through inheritance.','Using multiple monitors.','Writing code in multiple languages.','Compiling code twice.','A',10),(3779,'What is \'Method Overloading\'?','choose','Defining multiple methods with the same name but different parameters in the same class.','Defining the same method in a subclass.','Deleting a method.','Running a method too many times.','A',10),(3780,'What is \'Method Overriding\'?','choose','Providing a specific implementation of a method in a subclass that is already defined in its superclass.','Creating a new method name.','Calling a method from main.','Overloading operators.','A',10),(3781,'What is an \'Abstract Class\'?','choose','A class that cannot be instantiated and may contain abstract methods.','A class with no code.','A class that is invisible.','A final class.','A',10),(3782,'What is an \'Interface\' in Java/C#?','choose','A reference type containing only constants, method signatures, default methods, and static methods.','A graphical screen.','A class with variables.','A type of loop.','A',10),(3783,'What is \'Coupling\'?','choose','The degree of interdependence between software modules.','Connecting two cables.','Linking libraries.','Writing loops.','A',10),(3784,'What is \'Cohesion\'?','choose','The degree to which the elements inside a module belong together.','Sticking code together.','Using glue code.','Compiling code.','A',10),(3785,'Which is preferred in design: High Cohesion or Low Cohesion?','choose','High Cohesion.','Low Cohesion.','No Cohesion.','Random Cohesion.','A',10);
